/-!
# Negative-Sobolev time budget for actual finite Galerkin updates

The nonlinear estimate supplies a cutoff-independent `H⁻¹` mass, while the
exact viscous row pays the same mass with the vorticity-gradient ledger.
Combining them gives

```text
‖∂ₜω‖_{H⁻¹}²
  ≤ 8 M(u)² Y(ω) + 2 ν² (2π)² Z(ω).
```

The final source theorem integrates this inequality on the actual trajectory
generated by an arbitrary finite scale path.  Its bound reads only the
initial critical mass, viscosity, and the generated absorption coefficient;
it contains no mode count, maximum frequency, trajectory, time interval, or
analytic budget premise.

This is the compactness branch downstream of the exact mild identity.
Mathlib supplies Bochner integration and abstract compact operators, but no
ready torus Sobolev/Rellich/Aubin--Lions theorem.  Accordingly this module
closes the uniform `L²_t H⁻¹` derivative ledger and leaves subsequence
compactness as the next independent target consumer.
-/

